  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9305df3b-1002-478d-97ad-3ed95f6602c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 4.2.7 Recommendations Based on Lift\n",
    "\n",
    "Lift is particularly useful when selecting recommendation rules because it takes the general popularity of the products into account.\n",
    "\n",
    "A high-confidence rule is not necessarily interesting if the consequent product is already purchased very frequently. Lift helps identify rules where the consequent is substantially more likely when the antecedent is present.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, a rule with a lift clearly above 1 indicates a positive association between the antecedent and consequent.\n",
    "\n",
    "The company can use high-lift rules for targeted cross-selling, product bundles, and \"also buy\" recommendations.\n",
    "\n",
    "The strongest candidate rules should be evaluated using support, confidence and lift together rather than using one metric alone."
   ]
  },
